{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen","id":571984,"title":"About Possessions in Demon the Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-28T16:03:01-07:00","id":571984,"title":"About Possessions in Demon the Fallen","content":"Hello!<br /> It's a simple question about possession by demons of living hosts. I were wondering if it's possible for demons and humans to switch their personalities and stay booth conscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T16:06:06-07:00","id":571992,"title":"","content":"AFAIK, the Fallen is both the human AND the demon. They merge completely becoming a composite being. I may be wrong, but that's how we always ran it. Which is to say, they are both conscious, but there are not two consciousness. Just one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:02:08-07:00","id":572012,"title":"","content":"WHO HAS SUMMON THE ALMIGHTY CROWLEY!!!<br /> <br /> Oh, hi.<br /> <br /> On my games..the demon ACTS as the human but his personality is always in control (The demon one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:30:18-07:00","id":572027,"title":"","content":"The box has been open! Run!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T00:26:33-07:00","id":572374,"title":"","content":"Rules as writen say, that the demon merely poses as the Mortal, using inherited Memories and Feelings to instinktivly guide him though.<br /> In my chronicles however, I made them comlete hybrid beeings, similar to a mummy or a kami. It just flys better in my opinion, and gives us more of a reason, why and how the knowledge and feelings of the host are available to the demon.<br /> It also makes it easier to explain, how the body is still alive for any deamon, who doesn`t have Lore of Awakening 5, since the merger happens on the border of death, with the demon &quot;saving&quot; the hosts body, instead of waiting to reanimate a departed corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:15:51-07:00","id":573264,"title":"","content":"I thought the Fallen inhabit dying or psychologically compromised people, essentially hollowing out the mortal and taking up residence there as the host dies. There isn't any co-operation since there isn't actually two individuals comprising the Fallen, but vestiges of the human's memories, dreams and desires cling to the consciousness of the Demon, sometimes informing its actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T04:53:43-07:00","id":573734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=573264#post573264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Fallen inhabit dying or psychologically compromised people, essentially hollowing out the mortal and taking up residence there as the host dies. There isn't any co-operation since there isn't actually two individuals comprising the Fallen, but vestiges of the human's memories, dreams and desires cling to the consciousness of the Demon, sometimes informing its actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I read it as well. The Fallen seem to take people who are going to be effectivley gone anyway. People in comas, suicides and similar folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:40:05-07:00","id":573802,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the RAW says pretty exactly that.<br /> I actualy don`t like that version though, leading to my mentioned houserule. (See post above)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:59:15-07:00","id":574054,"title":"","content":"I would note that in the novels and the chapter-fiction, there are hints that the Human soul <b>CAN</b> sometimes linger.<br /> <br /> In the novels, Gaviel (the signature Devil) refers to and sometimes converses with what is left of Noah, his host, whose soul is buried deep beneath Gaviel's presence. In one of the chapter fictions for Time of Judgment, a Reconciler offers Lucifer some final advice, and then <i>vanishes</i>, leaving her human host in full possession of the body (though with muddled memories).<br /> <br /> For those reasons, I consider it sufficiently &quot;canon&quot; that a human soul could remain in the host body, just suppressed, slumbering, or fragmented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:01:33-07:00","id":576440,"title":"","content":"I went with that interpretation too regarding the human soul remaining and merging with the demon. It made it more interesting for me as a storyteller and for my player as well. It encouraged her to regard her &quot;host's&quot; life as her own. And put effort into keeping those human connections. It also made the whole scenario of the fallen poignant, and allowed the sympathetic fallen to be more sympathetic and the reprehensible ones truly horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T14:06:35-07:00","id":576757,"title":"","content":"I believe the Player's Guide actually talked about the different ways in how a demon could be in conflict with its host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T18:51:04-07:00","id":576970,"title":"","content":"When I STed my group for demon I always had them roll a d10, if they hit a threshold of 1-3 they were reg demon's out of the rule book, 4-6 they had a living human soul in there as well but the trauma from possession made them little more than background noise and sometimes when they botch we would fluff that it was because the human soul flipped out and someone took control of the body for a split second and made the character screw up, 7-8 you had a fully functional human soul in there with you that has it's own goals and desires and also open to pacts and such, 9-10 you merged perfectly with the human soul and regain 2 points of faith on your own at dawn as well as technically having the divine spark and such intact (players at the time didn't know it but the characters could have children).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T21:00:46-07:00","id":577060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=576970#post576970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I STed my group for demon I always had them roll a d10, if they hit a threshold of 1-3 they were reg demon's out of the rule book, 4-6 they had a living human soul in there as well but the trauma from possession made them little more than background noise and sometimes when they botch we would fluff that it was because the human soul flipped out and someone took control of the body for a split second and made the character screw up, 7-8 you had a fully functional human soul in there with you that has it's own goals and desires and also open to pacts and such, 9-10 you merged perfectly with the human soul and regain 2 points of faith on your own at dawn as well as technically having the divine spark and such intact (players at the time didn't know it but the characters could have children).</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it might do better as another splat dimension to add onto Houses. Then you could balance out the Faith boost with something for the more quiescent humans and &quot;demon in a corpse&quot; characters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:14:24-07:00","id":583897,"title":"","content":"About possession and mental illness: what if a demon took an autistic living vessel? The demon turn autistic himsef? Or the mental disease is healed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T20:28:15-07:00","id":584108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=583897#post583897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About possession and mental illness: what if a demon took an autistic living vessel? The demon turn autistic himsef? Or the mental disease is healed?</div> </div> </div> </div>i believe he heals up, the only catch comes with drug addicts or substance abusers . If i dont bad remember","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:13:50-07:00","id":584857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=583897#post583897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About possession and mental illness: what if a demon took an autistic living vessel? The demon turn autistic himsef? Or the mental disease is healed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Autism and the related mental states aren't an abnegation of the person's soul or a failure of their faith. They are complete human beings who have a different spectrum of perception and interaction. To say that these people are &quot;broken&quot; and therefore appropriate fodder for a demon looking for a damaged soul is pretty unpleasant. It's exactly like the mistake made by CtD where, at one time, the rules stated that autistic people were considered sources of Banality. If fully functioning autistic people are so empty and broken that demons can step in, how about homosexuals? After all, they were (and are still by some) considered to be mentally diseased. <br /> <br /> If a demon encountered an autistic person who had given way to absolute despair, etc. THEN that person would be a potential vessel. They are not excellent vessels merely due to being autistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:56:36-07:00","id":585048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=584857#post584857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Autism and the related mental states aren't an abnegation of the person's soul or a failure of their faith. They are complete human beings who have a different spectrum of perception and interaction. To say that these people are &quot;broken&quot; and therefore appropriate fodder for a demon looking for a damaged soul is pretty unpleasant. It's exactly like the mistake made by CtD where, at one time, the rules stated that autistic people were considered sources of Banality. If fully functioning autistic people are so empty and broken that demons can step in, how about homosexuals? After all, they were (and are still by some) considered to be mentally diseased.<br /> <br /> If a demon encountered an autistic person who had given way to absolute despair, etc. THEN that person would be a potential vessel. They are not excellent vessels merely due to being autistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallen made a similar mistake regarding autism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon core book, page 82</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mental instabilities like severe autism render the host incapable of truly exerting their free will, making them vulnerable.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But what about their souls? Are they also... weakly tethered?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Not so much weakly tethered as simply unable to assert their will in opposition to ours.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, as far as Demon is concerned, if you have what is presumably lower-functioning autism, then you're a potential empty vessel to the elohim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:14:31-07:00","id":586201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=585048#post585048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fallen made a similar mistake regarding autism.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, as far as Demon is concerned, if you have what is presumably lower-functioning autism, then you're a potential empty vessel to the elohim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it goes in the same category as pretty much the EXACT same thing as what happened in Changeling. It's total crap and needs to ignored, if not apologized for (not that there really is anyone who can apologize for it anymore.). It's a ghastly thing to put in a game. If that's the case, then Type 1 Bipolar people are fodder for possession. Almost every person with a schizoid disorder as well. Hell, anyone with epilepsy can go into that category. What about narcolepsy? People with serious ADD or ADHD or OCD? All the elderly with Alzheimers.... There are entire institutions full of people in permanent care that should just fill up with demons. <br /> <br /> Opening yourself to demonic possession should be all about &quot;dark moments of the soul&quot; and the human in question, failing to resist the siren seduction of something that &quot;will make it all better.&quot; Even for values of &quot;better&quot; that equal obliteration of self. Not in advancing an ideology of people with mental conditions being &quot;broken&quot; and perfect vessels for pure evil. <br /> <br /> Probably we'd have seen a tacit or explicit retraction of that position if Demon had a 2nd edition. I would certainly hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:54:22-07:00","id":586464,"title":"","content":"If the requirement is loss of will or sense of self, I'd say major clinical depression would be the primary true mental illness that renders a person vulnerable (although of course there are a wide variety of other mental disorders that can <i>result</i> in major depression). Alzheimer's sufferers would probably be in much the same boat; it's the ones who are so ground down by the disease that they give in to despair who become potential hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T09:34:28-07:00","id":587191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=586464#post586464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the requirement is loss of will or sense of self, I'd say major clinical depression would be the primary true mental illness that renders a person vulnerable (although of course there are a wide variety of other mental disorders that can <i>result</i> in major depression). Alzheimer's sufferers would probably be in much the same boat; it's the ones who are so ground down by the disease that they give in to despair who become potential hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur that the results of the condition in question might result in the necessary prerequisites for possession, not that the condition itself is a viable prerequisite. Which means that some of the &quot;targeted&quot; groups might actually be LESS likely to open to possession. Other conditions could produce equivalent despair as well. Becoming a parapeligic after a car wreck, for example. The despair over the loss of function could open the door, but it's NOT due to the loss of control itself. A lot of medications being used to treat conditions might make people more vulnerable as well, as much as recreational/avocational or self-medication use of such substances and their legal and illegal analogues may open the door. But it's a matter of choice as to whether the person lets to the demon in. Unless, I guess there IS no possibility of choice anymore due to the condition in question. Demons might be able to just step in to an empty brain in a still-living body. But even then, the case may be that the body is unresponsive but the individual's soul is largely intact, so the demon might need to get the requisite permission. Making someone in a permanent vegetative state aware of their situation could very well trigger the kind of conditions needed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:36:53-07:00","id":587240,"title":"","content":"If you want some real world ideas on possession, you should check out Coast to Coast AM with George Noory (Originally with Art Bell). There have been many shows about demon possession. Check out some of the shows at <a href=\"http://www.coasttocoastam.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.coasttocoastam.com/</a>.<br /> <br /> One of the best guests was Fr. Malachi Martin.(<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malachi_Martin\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malachi_Martin</a>) He talked at length about demon possession and its effects. He was once asked which city in the U.S. had the most demon possession. You would think like New York, Los Angeles or even Los Vegas, but he said the city in the U.S. with the most demon possessions was Louisville, KY. This show was back in the late 1990s, and at the time I was living in Lexington, KY. Now I live in Louisville, and I will tell you that there are a lot of things going on here. We have a very high murder rate. Every few days someone is killed. There is very high drug use, and a lot of domestic violence and abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":3684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","user":"David G","date":". 07-11-2015, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:33:07-07:00","id":587276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=587191#post587191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the case may be that the body is unresponsive but the individual's soul is largely intact, so the demon might need to get the requisite permission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there might be a misunderstanding here: <b>D:tF</b> has never treated permission as necessary for the demon to possess a human host. Some humans may choose to surrender themselves to a possessor, but it is not a prerequisite. The books present common circumstances of possession as cases where a person has been &quot;hollowed out&quot; by brain-death or severe injury (thus allowing the demon to slide in freely), or where their Will has been weakened by despair, illness, or abuse (and the demon can thus evict or dominate the host's soul).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T18:43:25-07:00","id":587591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=587240#post587240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the best guests was Fr. Malachi Martin.(<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malachi_Martin\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malachi_Martin</a>) He talked at length about demon possession and its effects. He was once asked which city in the U.S. had the most demon possession. You would think like New York, Los Angeles or even Los Vegas, but he said the city in the U.S. with the most demon possessions was Louisville, KY. This show was back in the late 1990s, and at the time I was living in Lexington, KY. Now I live in Louisville, and I will tell you that there are a lot of things going on here. We have a very high murder rate. Every few days someone is killed. There is very high drug use, and a lot of domestic violence and abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Memphis had more than three times the murders in 2014 with nearly the same population. The spirits I'd blame for that are Hennessy and 4 Loko, not Pazuzu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:36:19-07:00","id":587692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=587591#post587591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, Memphis had more than three times the murders in 2014 with nearly the same population. The spirits I'd blame for that are Hennessy and 4 Loko, not Pazuzu.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Your mother drinks Pabst in hell!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:59:13-07:00","id":594899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/571984-about-possessions-in-demon-the-fallen?p=576757#post576757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Player's Guide actually talked about the different ways in how a demon could be in conflict with its host.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> The Player's Guide p. 36-39 discusses manners in which a Fallen can possess a still living host:<br /> o Unclean Spirit (Mental Illness, Addiction, Brutal Living, Violent Trauma)<br /> o Free Will/Choosing Possession (Deal with the Devil, Occultism, Cultists)<br /> - logic being that unclean spirits have their will withered by the aforementioned activities and free will just requires the invitation and the method that invitation is presented.<br /> <br /> It further discusses the Human Soul in regards to possession:<br /> o Living Ghost (The human soul whispers in the demon's head, a lingering presence watching but unable to act)<br /> o Enslaved Soul (The demon coerces the soul, possibly extracting information, even Faith!)<br /> o Enslaved Demon (The human soul dominates the Demon; the Demon has no control but his voice urges the human to certain actions)<br /> o Drive the Soul out (The demon seeks to remove the human soul; technically, while never discussed, the reverse could happen)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}